# Box art drive for the landing-page games carousel (site/demos/box-art.mjs).
#
# The paddle FOLLOWS the pointer, so a Mouse.Move sweep is the whole drive.
# Coordinates are logical window points and the capture pins the window to
# 640x400, so the sweep below crosses the play field (x = 100..540) once every
# 60 frames — fast enough that the paddle is somewhere useful whenever the
# ball comes down, which is what keeps the rally (and the card) alive. Space
# launches, and is pressed again periodically so a lost ball relaunches instead
# of leaving a dead board.
#
#   functor -d examples/breakout run native --input-script boxart.script \
#     --script-dt 0.0166667 --capture-at-frame 150 --capture-frame /tmp/bo.png

